EXPERIMENT 6
Queries using Aggregate Functions, GROUP BY and HAVING

OBJECTIVE
To understand and implement SQL aggregate functions (COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX) along with GROUP BY and HAVING to summarize, group, and filter grouped data.

THEORY
Aggregate functions calculate a single summary value from a set of rows. GROUP BY creates summary rows for each group. HAVING filters groups after aggregation, whereas WHERE filters individual rows before grouping.

LOGICAL ORDER
FROM → WHERE → GROUP BY → HAVING → SELECT → ORDER BY

RESULT
The program demonstrates aggregate calculations, grouping, and filtering grouped results.

